{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "incident_inefficiency_reasons",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "issue_category_primary",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The type/category of the underlying issue (printer, hardware, software, connectivity) is a constitutive aspect OF what the recurring issue is -- it answers 'what kind of issue' as a part of the reason space."
    },
    {
      "name": "specific_issue_mechanism",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The specific failure mechanism (display_malfunction, paper_jam, network_outage) is a finer-grained aspect OF the issue itself, describing the concrete nature of the recurring problem."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_recurrence_pattern",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Recurrence pattern (repeated_device_type, systemic_pattern, single_mention) is an aspect OF the 'recurring' dimension of the reason -- it characterizes how the issue repeats, a constitutive facet of a recurring-issue concept."
    },
    {
      "name": "diagnostic_clarity",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "external_predictor",
      "rationale": "Whether the issue was clearly diagnosed is a property of the handling/resolution process, not a part OF the issue reason itself. It is an external factor affecting inefficiency rather than a constitutive aspect of the issue."
    },
    {
      "name": "assigned_technician_proxy",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "irrelevant",
      "rationale": "The identity of the assigned technician is a handler attribute (already largely present as assigned_to), not an aspect OF the issue reason. It is an external actor, not a facet of the concept, and risks being a restatement of existing columns."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": ["issue_category_primary", "specific_issue_mechanism", "issue_recurrence_pattern"],
  "non_facet_columns": ["diagnostic_clarity", "assigned_technician_proxy"],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.55,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.6,
  "rationale": "Three of the five columns are genuine facets of the recurring-issue concept: category (what type), mechanism (specific failure mode), and recurrence pattern (how it repeats). However, issue_category_primary and specific_issue_mechanism substantially overlap -- the mechanism values (display_malfunction, paper_jam, network_outage) are essentially finer instances of the same category dimension, so they carve largely the same aspect at two granularities, lowering mutual exclusivity. diagnostic_clarity is a process/handling attribute (external predictor of inefficiency) rather than a part of the issue reason, and assigned_technician_proxy is an external actor that restates an existing table column, so neither is constitutive. Exhaustiveness is moderate: the set captures the 'what/how' of issues but leaves out other constitutive aspects of inefficiency reasons such as knowledge/resource gaps, process/handoff friction, or root-cause layer, and the two non-facets consume slots without covering the concept."
}

